   "definition_quote": "We are given a compact arm set $\\mc{X}\\subset \\R^d$ with $\\mathrm{span}(\\mc{X})=\\R^d$ and an unknown reward vector $\\theta\\in\\R^d$. At each round $t=1,2,\\dots$, an algorithm selects an arm $x_t\\in\\mc{X}$ and observes $y_t=\\langle x_t,\\theta\\rangle+\\eta_t$, where $\\eta_t\\sim\\mc{N}(0,1)$. ... outputs $\\widehat{x}\\in\\mc{X}$ satisfying $\\P(\\max_{x\\in\\mc{X}}\\langle x-\\widehat{x},\\theta\\rangle\\le \\varepsilon)\\ge 1-\\delta$."
